Popular video meeting app Webex <a href="https://blog.webex.com/collaboration/webex-on-apple-iphone-duo-collaboration-that-moves-with-you/">was today updated</a> with support for Apple's <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a>. Webex works open or closed, in portrait or landscape mode, and even in a laptop or tent position.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/webex-app-iphone-duo.jpg" alt="" width="2100" height="1200" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1076654" /><br/>
When open, the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; shows more meeting participants, keeps shared content visible, and gives access to a whiteboard. Multitasking support allows Webex to be used alongside another app with Split View.<br/>
<br/>
Webex Mobile Camera Share lets users stream the iPhone's camera in a meeting when the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; is open in a laptop position, so participants can view the live camera feed and annotate it.<br/>
<br/>
Along with &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; support, Cisco has added the Webex Notetaker Agent to the iPhone app. It can transcribe and summarize in-person conversations and create action items.<br/>
